  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted → 0.5856 acc), the largest source of uncertainty is the RNA encoder choice, as it determines the quality of the single-cell representation fed into the multimodal model. config_012 is identical to config_009 in every setting except rna_encoder is changed from pca_n2000 (linear, 2000-dim) to scgpt (generative pretrained transformer for scRNA-seq), making this a clean single-variable A/B test. scgpt captures non-linear biological structure that PCA cannot, and if it yields a meaningful accuracy gain, it opens a rich sub-space of scgpt-based multimodal configurations to exploit in later experiments; if it does not improve, we can confidently rule out the RNA encoder as a bottleneck and redirect remaining budget toward fusion, aggregation, or image-encoder variations. Under an 8-experiment remaining budget, resolving this high-impact uncertainty early is the most information-efficient use of experiment 2."
